        "original_id": "a09bebf6-099d-54b4-8db7-65317b0edb52",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Entwistle\n- Organizations: The Who\n- Products: Tommy, Pinball Wizard, Overture, Underture, Sparks\n- Topics: chart performance, album release, instrumental tracks, band roles\n\nFacts:\n- The Who first released the double album Tommy in May 1969 as the band's fourth studio album.\n- In 1969, The Who released the original recording of \"Pinball Wizard\" as a single, and it reached No. 4 in the UK charts and No. 19 on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100.\n- On Tommy, \"Overture\" is one of three instrumental tracks, alongside \"Underture\" and \"Sparks\", although \"Overture\" includes some lyrics near the end.\n- John Entwistle was best known as the original bass guitarist for the English rock band The Who during a music career that spanned more than 40 years.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
